===Noun===
{{en-noun|skull and crossbones|skulls and crossbones}}

# An [[outline]] of a [[human]] [[skull]] and two [[crossed]] [[bone]]s; a [[symbol]] of [[death]] traditionally used on the [[Jolly Roger]], but now used as a [[warning]] on [[poison]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Practical handbook of industrial traffic management‎|page=579|author=Richard C. Colton|coauthors=|Edmund S. Ward, Charles H. Wager|year=1973|passage=When poisons are involved, red '''skull and crossbones''' are added.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The origin and early development of the Chinese writing system‎|page=16|author=William G. Boltz|year=1994|passage=The '''skull and crossbones''' is, to be sure, a visual sign that communicates a very specific meaning.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Madrid 1937: letters of the Abraham Lincoln Brigade from the Spanish|page=554|author=Cary Nelson|coauthors=Jefferson Hendricks|year=1996|passage=There was a big red cross in the center and around it were two '''skull and crossbones'''}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Street science: community knowledge and environmental health justice|page=182|author=Jason Corburn|year=2005|passage='''Skulls and crossbones'''- were used to label toxic storage sites}}

